# Ionity Installer GUI — scripts/README_INSTALLER.md

Purpose
- A conservative, auditable Tkinter-based GUI script to help users install common developer SDKs, CLIs and runtimes across Windows, macOS and Debian-based Linux.
- This updated version includes a broad set of programming languages and related tooling (see Languages section).

Safety and limitations
- Default mode: Dry-Run. The script will list the exact commands but will not execute them until you uncheck Dry-Run and confirm.
- You must explicitly accept a confirmation checkbox "I understand and accept" before the script will run commands.
- The script attempts to detect the OS and chooses appropriate command strings (winget/brew/apt). These are suggestions only — review them before executing.
- On Windows the script tries to request elevation if needed; on macOS/Linux it will check for root privileges and ask you to re-run with sudo if required.
- The script does NOT bundle or download installer binaries silently. For installers not available via the package manager (e.g. MATLAB, Delphi/Embarcadero), it offers to open the vendor download page instead.
- Test first in a disposable VM and audit the commands generated by the Dry-Run before executing.

Supported OSes (primary)
- Windows (winget preferred; falls back to guidance for other tools)
- macOS (Homebrew `brew`)
- Debian/Ubuntu Linux (apt). For other distros the script will display recommended commands.

