What the script does
- Presents a Tkinter GUI with checkboxes for each language/tool and common utilities.
- "Select All" and per-item selection available.
- "Preview commands" shows the exact commands the script would run for the selected OS.
- Dry-Run (default) mode lists commands but does not execute them.
- "Install" runs the commands item-by-item (only after explicit confirmation).
- For vendor-only installers, it opens the vendor download page instead of attempting unsafe automation.
- Logs all actions (timestamps, commands, stdout/stderr) to a log file in the repo root.

Usage example
1. Ensure Python 3.8+ is installed and Tkinter is available.
2. Run:
   python3 scripts/ionity_installer_gui.py
3. Use Dry-Run to preview commands. Check items to install, then check the "I understand and accept" checkbox and click "Install" to execute them.

Developer notes
- Commands are intentionally explicit strings returned by `get_commands_for_item()`. Edit those strings to adapt to your environments and package manager preferences.
- Maintain conservative behavior: Dry-Run default, explicit confirmation required.
- The script separates pseudo-actions (open_url:) vs shell commands. open_url: will be opened in the default browser.
- For any proprietary or paid software (MATLAB, Delphi, Visual Studio), the script will not download or install automatically; it opens vendor pages and provides recommended guidance lines.

